test(hydrofrac): demonstrate a false certificate from a total-loss clause

A run in which some domain fact vanishes at every member still yields a
clause (the union of the derivations of the pairs it *does* require), and
the search makes every later hypothesis hit it. That clause says nothing
about the vanished fact, so a hypothesis that breaks that fact *partially*
without touching the clause is never proposed.

- `suspected_total_loss_masks_a_partial_loss_certificate`: with
  `max_crashes(0)`, the search certifies `known` for zero crashes, while
  `omit(gossip m0→m1)` alone breaks it.
- `suspected_total_loss_masks_a_partial_loss_tolerance`: uncapped, the
  search reports a one-crash counterexample claiming zero crashes are
  tolerated.

Both tests assert the disagreement (they pass while the bug exists).
